    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d660">

                <pb facs="0704" n="690" xml:id="pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.30 Missions/11–2344: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-23T14:00:00-04:00">November 23,
                            1944—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1824. I strongly recommend that any official request by the Chilean Government
                    through diplomatic channels for the establishment of a United States naval
                    mission in Chile, if made, be approved by the Department and that the actual
                    establishment of a Naval Mission be expedited in every way possible. Since Naval
                        Attaché<anchor n="55" xml:id="d660-f1"/> is under instructions from Navy
                    Department not to take the initiative in this matter, no action will be taken by
                    Embassy until instructions are received from Department (Reference Navy
                    Department’s confidential serial 015417, July 1 this year<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d660-f2"/>). However the Naval Attaché was recently informed
                    unofficially by two Chilean Navy Captains that Chilean Navy anticipated
                    requesting such a mission in the near future in response to which Capitan
                    Rockwell intimated that matter would be given every consideration in Washington
                    if the request were made (see Naval Attaché serial 0941 to Chief Naval
                    Operations dated November 15<anchor n="56" xml:id="d660-f3"/>). In Rockwell’s
                    opinion Admiral Merino, Commander-in-Chief of Chilean Navy, may shortly bring up
                    question officially.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
